{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/8520-werewolf-the-forsaken-instincts-the-early-incarnation-of-an-overhaul","id":8520,"title":"Werewolf: the Forsaken Instincts; the early incarnation of an overhaul.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-11T18:32:15-08:00","id":8520,"title":"Werewolf: the Forsaken Instincts; the early incarnation of an overhaul.","content":"Some of y'all were curious what I was rambling on about with the Instincts we were working on between myself and my co-ST for the game we've been running some years. So far as the first draft this is what we've came up with and are deciding to use/playtest to see how they pan out; they're not perfect, and no doubt they'll need further refinement. This is derived from watching things play out, player input and ongoing tweaks and house rules and finding the light approach just wasn't enough for what we wanted in our game. This is the (tentative) results of that, one part at least given the numerous other areas we're tackling with some player input. Luckily they're used to ongoing tweaks; the game has been rolling for years, so we've had to dig into things as they've came up.<br /> <br /> It should be noted these are predicated on quite a few changes to the game.<br /> <br /> <i>Renown is being reworked into a Status mechanic for Tribes and Auspices and has no impact on power caps, nor Instinct dice rolls. It doesn't impact overall honorary spirit rank; that's being dovetailed into Primal Urge. It -does- have some supernatural impacts to the character (which will be discussed later when we've come to more of a consensus) but this is a big paradigm shift; it won't be touching Gifts. Gifts right now is the term used for when a spirit part of a Totem/Spirit Pact grants the individual minor blessings. There is no cap on Instincts.<br /> <br /> Essence is -not- gained from Loci; they're certainly areas where resonant essence spills most freely into the Shadow, but there are no more &quot;werewolf loci farming&quot;. They're areas that, like a body of water in the woods still attract ample prey; spirits, and in turn they're still considered prime areas to have as territory and to keep an eye out for trouble. That said, you get your essence for hunting and feasting; spirits, humans, wolves, werewolves, and rarely much else. None for your Auspice. No Essence batteries for the half-fleshed. They're hunters, so they hunt for their fuel stat.<br /> <br /> Spirit Numina replace gifts. They're not part of &quot;sets&quot; rather than individually bought, though we're thinking a Werewolf may be able to gain equivalents by incorporating/learning a portion of another's Influence. Trophies, scars and other supernaturally altering bits from Werewolves successfully hunting down spirits (and in some cases other werewolves and spiritual critters).<br /> <br /> It's possible to trick or barter for them but that's usually the exception for Forsaken; they're not liked by the Shadow and to have your Essence and Resonance altered in that way to make your spiritual side manifest a Numina by a spirit outside of hunting means, you guessed it, you may be changing more than you bargained for taking some of the concepts presented in the Chronicler's Guide. They're still in the game, they're just not the default power set (though most characters will have the Materialize numina save as a means to dematerialize and pass through the gauntlet). Obviously many won't translate directly, given the half-fleshed werewolves nature, and some might just be outside their ability to learn without other events in place. Still, they're not the primary nor relied about sets. We'll be presenting some ideas and systems for this later on.<br /> <br /> Rites are still around. However, they will no longer be a random grab-bag of powers that didn't fit within a Gift set or the absolute mess they were before. They're not going be using Harmony as the primary way to perform them mechanically. They're going to reflect more finesse based Essence and Resonance manipulation and weeded out and tweaked to reflect that. Rites are the funky spirit arts of Werewolves that can use the fundaments the Shadow is built on for some of the funky effects they had before. Once we have more functionally fleshed out we'll share these notions, but it's still a system being discussed. Instincts more readily reflect the Influence of a werewolf. Their base &quot;Numina&quot; to look at them at a spiritual POV is their innate powers; shapeshifting, regeneration, etc. Purely social rites will not require a purchase under this system; they become cultural traditions of the various Tribes.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Dalu and Urshul are not accessible by default without further Shapeshifting Instincts; most will consider this a debuff. Once again, there's some reasons for this we'll explain in later documents once we start putting them together with Instincts. Dalu gets some minor changes. This is definitely something specific to our game; I doubt we'd see this alteration in Idigam Chronicles.</i><br /> <br /> The basic structure works like this; each Instinct has a passive effect that, as it is raised increases a facet of being a werewolf. Getting better at pursuing prey; more time in Gauru; easier time shapeshifting under duress and so on. Each level (1-5, consider them &quot;Honings&quot;) starts small, subtle, and then increases in magnitude.<br /> <br /> Many are Reflexive and require no rolls; Instincts are primarily quick and responsive or capitalizing on already present facets of being a Werewolf. Some do require rolls, but most that bolster oneself simply cost Essence and in some instances Willpower. This is intentional; myself and my co-ST don't want to arbitrarily toss down Dice rolls for their powers without need unless the power specifically targets someone beyond the werewolf (and therefore resisted or contested), or would better served with a success basis.<br /> <br /> 1-3 are primarily internalized unless an instinct predicated on affecting others like Dominance, usually bolstered by the passive bonus. They're the major portion of the Instincts; 4-5's are just gravy, 1-3 is your reliable tool-set and should cover all the major bases of the Instincts theme. You shouldn't be racing to get the most utility running for 4-5s.<br /> <br /> 4 is where you start to see further refinement of the existing themes into a stronger effect or unexpected permutations of an Instinct, and 5 is generally where one sees a &quot;What the hell, I didn't know they could do that?&quot; sort of effect. Sometimes this simply changes what lower Honings are capable of; other times it shows one inflicting their Instinct onto their environment or other entities in frightening ways. We took quite a bit of nod from the ideas presented in Blood and Smoke regarding progression and aggregate effects.<br /> <br /> We assume that there may be additional Instincts out there (particularly among the Pure), and that there may be individual Honings that branch out from the standard 1-5 (think more like Promethean Transmutations, or Single Level Devotions) but right now we wanted the bread and butter covered. Right now, they don't rely on spirits being part of the game focus; they work on any viable target provided they're in the same state/plane of existence. You can use Dominance as readily upon a human as you can a Changeling as you can a Spirit. I'd say overall they are more potent than many of the prior Gifts overall, less so in a few instances, though not as broken as quite a few were (not to say they couldn't turn out to be broken in brand new ways mind you). They need cleaning up, as well as later expansion, both to address The Pure and additional diversity. They definitely need tweaking in a lot of areas and some have already been rewritten, no doubt with more Honings requiring that.<br /> <br /> Every werewolf will have Feral Instincts and Shapeshifting Instincts as an affinity; each Tribe has a particular Instinct they tend to focus on and learn more readily that helps bolster their practices and assumptions. The Blood Talons treat Rage as affinity. Bone Shadows treat Sensory as theirs. Hunters in Darkness treat Territoriality as their big thing. Iron Masters treat Stealth as theirs and Storm Lords emphasize Dominance. Others may learn these Instincts as non-affinity costs. Right now for the quick and dirty until their individual Instinct is done, the Ivory Claws treat Dominance as theirs, and the Predator Kings treat Territoriality as affinity and the Fire-Touched Rage (odd choices I know, but there are reasons for it we'll get into later). Odds are with these you'll see some funky ideas like Rabid Instincts, Purity Instincts and Savagery Instincts with some nods to their existing sets; more likely than not these are just complete sets of &quot;alternate honings&quot; from the base one that they developed an affinity over time over the &quot;originals&quot;. We originally debated a Passive effect to each individual level; this proved far too unwieldy thoguh.<br /> <br /> Obviously we wouldn't mind input on these, how to clean them up, tweak them or otherwise change them with better options. We have our own player input, but the more ideas the better to getting the final form to gel. That said; don't waste our time with &quot;you shouldn't use these at all. Go back to the old core W:tF setup.&quot; type of comments please; it's not happening, and not constructive to what we're trying to do.<br /> <br /> The first I'll present for you folks is Feral Instincts; it's based around the Father Wolf Gift set and primarily addresses a lot of innate physical/feral nuances of werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":".  some minor cleaning up. Brain fried large posts are fried. 11-12-2013, 12:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T18:40:19-08:00","id":8525,"title":"","content":"Right now Feral Instincts is very internalized; unlike quite a few of the others made it's level 5 does not start to outwardly affect one's environment or others overtly, save in how readily they can be hunted and consumed for Essence. It's subtler in that fashion comparatively; that said it does make for Shadow and material world survival challenges to find food and keep supernaturally empowered much easier than others; we'd imagine quite a few very high Primal Urge werewolves go for the pinnacle of it to have easy times surviving in both worlds with less actual problems. Hunting less, eating less, fewer issues with oddball Resonance as often and so on.<br /> <br /> Dealing Aggravated Damage -currently- is omitted from the power sets until we see enough precedent otherwise; you can inflict Lethal on individuals who'd normally downgrade that type of damage from claws and fangs with Savage Rending now, along with some other bonuses. We're strictly leaving Aggravated Damage to 'wrap-arounds' and the actual supernatural banes that inflict such; there won't be many powers that specifically do that as a result. In most instances it will be Numina that may allow for such in appropriate instances when it comes to fire and other banes that inflict Aggravated on the appropriate supernatural; silver however, is right out. It's being treated spirit-wise as far more predisposed against werewolves than many spirits that already have an abject distaste and fear of them. It's debatable if a werewolf could even properly consume a spirit of silver to gain it's Numina or a distilled effect of an Influence of it; its entire resonance is likely entirely incompatible but there may be ways in the form of plot hooks. I just don't want it a default assumption; it's bane, their one innate one; it shouldn't have any sort of easy use or pass on a supernatural level.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":114,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","user":"Tatterdemalion King","date":". 11-12-2013, 12:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T18:58:35-08:00","id":8535,"title":"","content":"Shapeshifting Instincts currently uses much of Mother Luna Gift Listings. As mentioned in the initial post one house-rule that's in place is that Dalu and Urshul are -not- part of the default werewolf package, so keep this in mind. Primal Form got switched to Level 4; it's now more versatile (though needs some tweaking) and allows you to push your alternate forms past their usual shapeshifting limits, creating customized forms.<br /> <br /> We're still a bit iffy on how to reflect the bonuses of Skin Stealing; scent transferred before, but right now that's part of Stealth; there may still be bonuses towards that worth adding in, but the idea is that for wolves and werewolves scent is a ridiculously important sense to determine individuality and identity; things that play around with that should specifically fall in line with Stealth, not shapeshifting alone. This could be changed, of course.<br /> <br /> The level 5 is something I wanted to see back in the werewolf power sets for a long time; you had vampire powers that played around with the embrace with certain bloodlines (those suicide kings and queens I totally forget the name of right now) and we figured the pinnacle of Shapeshifting should be control over the form of -others-. Also needing some cleaning up, durations and trigger explanations, but basically, turning someone temporarily into something more like a classic werewolf? That's the one that does it. Locking others away from other forms for a time? That too. You'll notice that a lot of the level 5s are quite potent, and that's entirely intentional. Shapeshifting is where you first start to see how various levels/'honings' can influence one another into funky combinations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T19:06:45-08:00","id":8539,"title":"","content":"Dominance Instincts; the desire to be at the pinnacle of a pack, an alpha, to have others fall into line and work as a cohesive unit under your own influence. I absolutely along with my Co-ST did -not- want it to be a limited Dominate redux so folks will notice it doesn't quite run in the same way, be it old or new. It still can affect groups of people; that's part of the point, this is the Instinct that most certainly allows leaders of their packs to enforce their will on others.<br /> <br /> At 5 you can -force- others to become temporary members of an &quot;artificial pack&quot; to aid you. At lower levels it starts with the dominant werewolf being able to act the part and stand their ground more readily than most (how else do you become such a leader? Certainly by not being a spinless pushover or easily influenced; then you're just a puppet). A lot of it pushes the angle of making others &quot;submit&quot; to you rather than direct overt control. 4 amplifies this idea; you become such a dominant (and frightening) individual that others hesitate to actively threaten you.<br /> <br /> As always, it could use some more tweaking; there was a lot of initial redundancy that had to be heavily re-jiggered, and it may still require a bit more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T19:19:36-08:00","id":8542,"title":"","content":"The current Rage Instincts resembles a mix between the Strength and old Rage set, though with some stark changes here and there. The level 5 is probably the most unexpected of the lot; being able to create infectious Rage in others that spread through violence while the werewolf source is able to designate who's safe from the furious wildfire. Divide and conquer. Lower levels also use some inspiration from a Cahalith gift from Signs of the Moon where you grow in fury the more you kill. We've debated adjusting the Initiative bonuses to something else or retweaking, but the base effects is what we want. The trouble is keeping it from turning into an overwhelming bonus; the idea however that the more pain you suffer, the more you get angry, and the angrier you get the more vicious seems like a good idea. Lower levels address that those who hone their Rage can push themselves to more uses of Gauru outside of Death Rage.<br /> <br /> One thing to note; we are having that your Stamina + Primal Urge turns aren't a hard cap; any additional turns in Gauru past your grace period add a cumulative -1 Penalty on top of your initial Gauru penalties to avoid Death Rage. The further you push, the more likely you are to rage. Rage Instincts doesn't obliviate this (it seemed to be counterintuitve), but certainly lets you get more out of it. It's not a power set that generally makes you directly tougher; that's Feral Instincts right now; it does however make you much deadlier in conflict and tearing the shit out of things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T19:26:10-08:00","id":8551,"title":"","content":"Next we have Sensory Instincts; tapping into ones ability to perceive and understand ones surroundings more effectively. It starts with a heightened more precise danger-sense and eventually becomes the ability to track someone or their property to an insane degree like the old Find Path (which was one extraordinarily potent Gift in my and my co-STs experience) while you're on the same plane of existence. At 3 you gain a very, very strong level of perception regarding hidden nuances of the supernatural; odds are Werewolves will still be able to sense when they enter a Loci's area of influence innately, however this one will give much more precise information than the generalities from that. Level 4 is more akin to an amped up Sense Weakness; there's a reason why Bone Shadows really favour this Instinct and hopefully it shows.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T19:33:22-08:00","id":8556,"title":"","content":"Stealth Instincts; amplifying the instincts to effectively move quietly, unseen and more effectively avoid danger or ambush prey. It avoids a lot of overt things like direct invisibility or mental false images; again we didn't want this to be too much like a vampire's Obfuscate or some aspects of the Contract of Smoke. While level 4 might not seem potent (at first) it's worth keeping in mind the idea of shapeshifters as trickster figures at times; leaving the physical evidence of someone else at your choice? Talk about incrimination and falsified crimes. Got an opponent who's blinded? Change your scent to their packmates, and their packmates to yours and see how things go. It's intended to be versatile, potentially frightening. Use that in tandem with Shapeshifting Instincts and you may see where we were going with it.<br /> <br /> Level 5 does have on effect that is a &quot;soft&quot; memory wipe; given we're not using Lunacy in the old fashion but instead using the Predatory Aura to cover making others feel like prey, acting irrationally etc. it was here it seemed to have a better place; at the pinnacle, people don't even remember the details of you being around or what you were with proper clarity without rolls among the other effects it amplifies. This one had a -lot- of tinkering as an Instinct; it still likely needs more, but the level 1 is something we've wanted for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T19:42:51-08:00","id":8559,"title":"","content":"Territorial Instincts primarily plays upon the Predatory Aura; that being said, we're still hashing out the mechanics behind it, and we're wanting to divide it up into 3 aspects much like Blood and Smoke does; a physical one, that's all about making an individual wish to flee and feel like prey, having trouble to actions that don't emphasize that; one that impacts the mental with a break down of the rational mind, going somewhat feral; and another for the social that may play up the whole &quot;animalistic dangerous magnetism&quot; aspect to reflect getting mates, or perhaps to reinforce ones position as the dominant predator. If the latter there may be some tweaks to Dominance Instincts.<br /> <br /> Right now it uses the ideas of a few gifts along with the notion of Warding; it's all about marking things, people and places as yours and getting increasingly more impact on that, from tracking the marked things down, to warding others off, defending them with increased fervor and efficiency, knowledge of the areas tied to you and later broader influences on those within your territory. It's still very rough, but it has some potential.<br /> <br /> That's the last of the ones we have complete as is, what do you all think, and what areas would you tweak mechanically or otherwise? These are just the basics mind you; as I sad, no alternate levels (yet), no Pure specific Instincts just yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T20:46:01-08:00","id":8578,"title":"","content":"I was skeptical at first, but after reading the drafts, I'm digging this. Definitely an improvement from the standard gift system.<br /> <br /> Note: Your Stealth Instincts link leads to the Sensory Instincts draft.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/542-witch","name":"Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T20:53:48-08:00","id":8583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Witch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/8520-werewolf-the-forsaken-instincts-the-early-incarnation-of-an-overhaul?p=8578#post8578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was skeptical at first, but after reading the drafts, I'm digging this. Definitely an improvement from the standard gift system.<br /> <br /> Note: Your Stealth Instincts link leads to the Sensory Instincts draft.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed, should take you to the actual Stealth Instincts now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-11T21:02:32-08:00","id":8584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve gone with a much simpler implementation: \u201cAll Good Gifts\u201d from <b>Forsaken Chronicler\u2019s Guide</b>, with \u201cGifts\u201d renamed as \u201cInstincts\u201d and buyable with experience points, without any need to involve spirits. More traditional Gifts are also available, using the houseruled patches found on the forums; acquisition is done with \u201cSpirit Predation\u201d (also <b>Forsaken Chronicler\u2019s Guide</b>, but is not capped by Renown; nor do Gifts come free with Renown.</div> </div> </div> </div>We were originally looking at doing that, and honestly we're using some portions of those ideas for Totem blessings and the like. Spirit Predation we're likely tweaking quite a bit, but we didn't find just adopting those sections wholesale from the Chronicler's Guide honestly to be enough for what we wanted. We've got the books; we just used them as a stepping off point to go further to plunk down what we wanted to have (and would purchase as powers if we were playing) and that of our players. The suggestions there weren't -quite- what we were after wholesale, though in a few places the were in good part.<br /> <br /> For the record, we're using those &quot;Cursed&quot; type of werewolves more akin to the classic ideas from the Chronicler's Guides as the fleshy counterpart to the usual nasty spirit offspring. They're problematic, though for very differing reasons than their spirit brethren in our setting. They're great books, but given GMC and further reading we're not just adopting them as written unless the material fully jives with what we had in mind. We're not afraid to rewrite and tinker even if it creates a ridiculous amount of additional work at times. They're inspiration and sometimes culled from but, eh. We came to the conclusion that overall we were better off just writing directly with what we and our players had in mind rather than backtracking too consistently towards them and not seeing what we could fashion ourselves if that makes sense. Not so much reinventing the wheel as &quot;Is this wheel the right size for our chronicle car?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T01:19:29-08:00","id":8669,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I\u2019ve gone with a much simpler implementation: \u201cAll Good Gifts\u201d from <b>Forsaken Chronicler\u2019s Guide</b>, with \u201cGifts\u201d renamed as \u201cInstincts\u201d and buyable with experience points, without any need to involve spirits. More traditional Gifts are also available, using the houseruled patches found on the forums; acquisition is done with \u201cSpirit Predation\u201d (also <b>Forsaken Chronicler\u2019s Guide</b>, but is not capped by Renown; nor do Gifts come free with Renown.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, this is gold.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T02:52:07-08:00","id":8692,"title":"","content":"Where's the Predatory Aura write-up?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T03:56:03-08:00","id":8707,"title":"","content":"I do like these Instincts... Some feedback?<br /> <br /> Feral instincts mentions canines a lot, shouldn't lupines also be mentioned? :P<br /> <br /> In the Shapeshifting instricts, the conditions at the end don't have a &quot;sources&quot; section, I think adding those would be useful for imagining where they can come from.<br /> <br /> Dominance, I think that there should be a carrot to the stick of the packminded condition. Even a small bonus to teamwork or actions that directly benefit the group would be good.<br /> <br /> I like the sensory stuff, I take it B&amp;S auspex played an inspiring part?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T04:53:22-08:00","id":8727,"title":"","content":"Well, wolves are a type of canine, I didn't think there was much need to get too redundant in term use; I wanted the ability to affect canines as a whole (including wild dogs and similar things for werewolves in regions that host them rather than wolves) to present that a werewolf is going to be top of the canine food chain when they play around with that. And yeah, the Sources inclusion hasn't been added yet; we're going back to plunk them in, but we didn't feel they were a priority with the initial draft. It's something to plunk in when we go back over them. Honestly it was the easy part; we focused on getting past the hard part first, so it's obviously still needing completion in some areas.<br /> <br /> With Pack Minded and a carrot; I agree there, we've just not figured out a concise way to do it. Originally it had a nod towards that but it came out too muddled in explanation so it just got deleted out some time back. If you have a suggestion there it would be greatly appreciated; I really think it'd benefit from something like that. There was originally a teamwork bonus; right not it benefits from the Pack Bond merit we've been tooling around with which does give an incentive like that (provided the user has it), but I could see an ingrained bonus working better for the power as long as it's not too much; it's a pretty potent effect; it's been down-toned from the first brainstorming sessions but may have lost something in doing so.<br /> <br /> Auspex was heavy inspiration for Sensory; we didn't want it the same, obviously, but treating things more of a 'questions asked' system overall seemed the right direction so we didn't throw the mechanics teased about Auspex entirely out just for the sake of being different. Q&amp;A really seems to be the ideal format for those types of powers.<br /> <br /> After playing around with the idea (and having long since used things like the Mekhet Dreams merit in the past and present) it seemed like a good starting point to go from so there's definitely some overlap compared to say, looking at the old Dominance gifts and comparing them to the old Dominate. Dominance I think diverges heavily; Sensory has been a tougher nut to crack. Some of the questions and presentation still needs some tinkering mind you; it's definitely not polished and complete, but I -think- it's going the right direction. Initially it was a different sense per &quot;honing&quot; that was affected for the earlier levels, but it seemed too cludgy to break it down that way along with Stealth so you get what you now have as a result. All of them could have their descriptions written in a more concise way, and more cleanly to boot. <br /> <br /> The game we run is one where information -really- is power and extraordinarily important; I guess you could say it has some tugs toward Call of Cthulhu with investigation given all the player handouts and the level of mystery and hidden information in our setting, so we definitely wanted werewolves to have a strong set of investigation tools for what they consistently run up against. We've got quite a few plot-lines started over 5 years ago that only now are getting the surface scratched as new and old PCs have dug up information; we wanted to make sure sensory got a lot of love as a result especially considering when we think wolves (and werewolves) we think expert hunters, trackers and supernaturally sensory acute. I'm hoping what's there will do the trick without stepping on Auspex's toes too badly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T06:18:18-08:00","id":8750,"title":"","content":"Yeah, the inspiriation is clear, but I like the question you can ask. They are themed towards werewolf which is nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/417-the_duck","name":"the_duck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar417_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T18:29:22-08:00","id":9377,"title":"","content":"<i>&quot;Territorial Instincts primarily plays upon the Predatory Aura; that being said, we're still hashing out the mechanics behind it, and we're wanting to divide it up into 3 aspects much like Blood and Smoke does; a physical one, that's all about making an individual wish to flee and feel like prey, having trouble to actions that don't emphasize that; one that impacts the mental with a break down of the rational mind, going somewhat feral; and another for the social that may play up the whole &quot;animalistic dangerous magnetism&quot; aspect to reflect getting mates, or perhaps to reinforce ones position as the dominant predator. If the latter there may be some tweaks to Dominance Instincts.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> The Predatory Auras aren't in a state to be posted just yet, odd given an Instinct that runs off them is roughly completed, I know. Hopefully they should be set within the next few days; what's been bandied about so far hasn't been set into a hard mechanic we want to test out. Same basic idea though, A power Attribute + Primal Urge and standard costs, backing down or fighting in with failed attempts to fight it causing a bonus to the Werewolf to pursue the actions in line with the aura against the individual who gains the condition. I'm not sure about the 1 month duration; it'll depend on what the overall potency of these are. They'll still affect individuals, not groups. I really want to present the &quot;You're my prey&quot; physical one as a good tactic to isolate others from the &quot;herd&quot;.<br /> <br /> The rough idea is similar to b&amp;s until we get something more evocative; Individuals suffer a -2 penalty to composure actions beyond fleeing and defending themselves (for the Physical Prey condition) in general if unable to flee, the werewolf gets +2 in pursuit of hunting their quarry and considers 3 successes exceptional successes in this area (the werewolf specifically, not anyone pursuing them). That's the rough mechanic, but I'd prefer to tweak it more. It may actually have the penalty to -any- action beyond fleeing but I'm not sure that's the way to go. It'd be a sense of overwhelming terror that one is -prey- regardless of how they fight or struggle.<br /> <br /> The Irrational one (Mental) would involve actions that require complex thought and memory; you could see it as a mix of PTSD and ones instincts overriding the rational mind. I'm not so sure how much it will resemble the former (assuming the former is kept) where you suffer a -2 Penalty to most Memory rolls and Mental Skills or something to do with Extended rolls; I want to have something that reflects the mind buckling under a wash of instinct and/or fear that isn't just flight. I've been debating with my Co-ST if this should reflect some sort of Lunatic condition instead, a bit more madness-like.<br /> <br /> The social idea is to present that &quot;werewolves have a dangerous allure between their exceptional health, the latent danger etc.&quot; that's been bandied about various books. I'd rather it wasn't a direct port over of Wanton, or it may be worth keeping it as a more direct fear affect; the physical aura more towards pursuit and fighting back, the social more towards fleeing? They all need some more thought and potentially differing mechanics; I'm not a big fan of the social one as a lure; predatory seduction seems more of a vampire thing given their nature than a werewolf, but like I said, all these ideas are very, very rough right now. I'd prefer that all of them in one way or another pushed the sense of being prey more, and in how it's presented alters the reaction via a Condition. This could mean some tweaks to Territorial Instincts as a result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-13T01:50:51-08:00","id":9533,"title":"","content":"I'd call it something else, given that's the vamp's mechanic. Predator's Menace was thrown around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T08:10:20-08:00","id":12741,"title":"","content":"@Tatterdemalion King: Would you mind if I used these in one of my own games, with a few tweaks?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/542-witch","name":"Witch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T14:51:16-08:00","id":12983,"title":"","content":"By all means. Keep in mind they've not been thoroughly playtested yet so there's going to be some possible hiccups. We went back and fiddled with them more than once already but without getting our crew using them yet (that'll likely start next month if all goes as planned) I've got a feeling a couple areas may need some additional thought. If you run into an Instinct that has a hiccup/rough spots/muddled descriptions or redundancies, give me a heads up, it may expedite streamlining them further into a complete final draft.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-17T17:11:20-08:00","id":13067,"title":"","content":"Hot damn, this is just what I've been looking for. My early draft for a Werewolf rewrite was different in structure, but this fits the bill. I'll tweak it for myself and see if I can get something up and running. Thanks for sharing!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T09:26:51-08:00","id":13437,"title":"","content":"Hmm\u2026 the more I look these over, the more I like them. I\u2019m thinking of using them not just for Uratha, but also for Dire Beasts (unusually dangerous animals with velociraptor-like intelligence and augmented physical abilities; the Instincts nicely cover many of the augmentations).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-18T09:57:46-08:00","id":13458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/8520-werewolf-the-forsaken-instincts-the-early-incarnation-of-an-overhaul?p=9533#post9533\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd call it something else, given that's the vamp's mechanic. Predator's Menace was thrown around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Menace of the Hunter? Menace for short.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>- If you must be ridiculous, I must ridicule you.<br /> - Those that can give up essential liberties in exchange for temporary safety deserve neither liberty nor safety. -- Benjamin Franklin</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/375-papa-bear","name":"Papa Bear","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar375_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1920"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-20T10:13:08-08:00","id":14777,"title":"","content":"Primal Menace has a certain ring to it as well. Honestly though, the name of the Predatory Aura (and it's necessity on being differently named) is next to nil; from an out-of-game perspective just calling it Predatory Aura as a mechanic to reflect supernatural predators and what they display with some consistency works well enough to reflect who has it and who doesn't. I doubt werewolves (or vampires) would really put much thought into it and naming conventions when it something that's effectively an instinct-driven reaction/action any more than &quot;Touchstones&quot; would be an in-game reference bandied about. <br /> <br /> I'm more concerned with Territorial Instincts having enough 'oomph' using it as a basis for some of the effects and if durations get fiddled around with, how that will impact it as well. It may require quite a bit more fiddling, and the Predatory Aura is going to require a bit of looking at in relation with stacking or interactions with Dominance at the early levels. I could see tweaking them, possibly another instinct to reflect an enhancement of one of the 3 Attributes used to spring board from there but that could be unnecessary. I'm still in the mind that breaking them up into a Prey condition (for the Strength using Aura manifestation), Lunatic (for the Intelligence based one showing the break down of the rational mind) and something like Broken-Willed (already using the terms submissive and cowed; for the Presence based, easy enough to rename conditions though). <br /> <br /> If we use the existing examples as fairly intact, you can only get hit with one of these once a month; will Territorial then bypass this restriction when folks start messing with your stuff? Given the Resolutions for the examples it may not need to, but this requires some thought. I'm thinking the Aura needs to be kept pretty straight forwards; I don't think it should affect groups (you're on average running in a pack anyhow, and it's been mentioned Teamwork may handle the pack going after someone anyhow with these at increased intensity). Duration wouldn't have a timer; simply the resolution. Less fuss and muss.<br /> <br /> This would mean on average someone wanting to fuck around with a marked subject via that Instinct would be needing to spend a Willpower to avoid backing off and leaving it be if the werewolf's Primal Urge was higher than their supernatural power stat (so mortals in general would -have- to spend Willpower to try). The usual contested roll with the appropriate Attribute + Power Stat in response (and the condition cannot be 'reflected back' upon the Instinct user) and if failing, the condition. The werewolf gets a +2 bonus to dicking the affected individual with exceptional successes on 3 rather than 5. The instinctive terror/irrationality/submission of the affected individual is -2 penalty to select rolls. Using Competitive as a basis one could look at how Willpower could interact; the Presence based aura may be the place for this.<br /> <br /> I'm imagining the werewolf will know who messed with their shit if they run into them at the lower levels; if they gain the condition, the werewolf who inflicted it knows it was -them- who did so otherwise it loses some clout. This is being added to the clean draft, and some prelim Aura mechanics will be up soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T01:35:33-08:00","id":15241,"title":"","content":"If it's named exactly the same, this means it's the exact same mechanic. It means vampires and werewolves might confuse each-other upon sensing one another as fellow predators. It makes for awkwardness.<br /> <br /> Fluff-wise? You have a race of creatures who's naming conventions is -heavily- influenced by the alien tongue of the spirits. (Oh, I forgot you wanna nix those as well. Oh well.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T12:55:08-08:00","id":15547,"title":"","content":"It's not a priority until the mechanics are fleshed out further. When we say &quot;predatory aura&quot; right now, everyone knows what it's intended to refer to conceptually given the actual system isn't set yet. When it's finalized, sure, it can be changed in name but it's just not important enough as is to worry about as a &quot;big thing&quot; until something gels more. It's not likely to be bandied about in-character, and out of character it doesn't need a divergent name yet. Not on my priority list, I'll worry about what name rings the best later on and what my co-ST and players also chime in on and more get bandied about.<br /> <br /> As for spirits; they're not excised and thrown out. If the were, there wouldn't be an entire section of the Shadow being worked on, let alone the big things on hunting spirits. They just aren't as integral to everything and being far more take-it-or leave it in varying amounts rather than being written right into every basic power. It's still a major part of the setting and a common antagonist set, but the system and setting idea shifts don't make them an essential aspect to worry about if the ST's/players aren't interested in it. The Shadow and spirits is treated more akin to the Hedge and hobgoblins to use a comparison; it's present, it can overlap on a lot of areas, it can be ridiculously important to an individual chronicle but you don't need to focus on it for how you get your powers, or what's going to be going on in the average game. It's just going to be easier to ignore it entirely if it's not an area one wants to mess with.<br /> <br /> You don't -need- Totems to form a &quot;proper&quot; pack in this setup . You don't -need- spirits to gain your main power set (though you can get Numina in addition to these if you decide to). You don't -need- Loci, but if you're playing around with Totems, want consistent spirits to hunt (think watering hole) consistently for essence/numina, odds are you're going to want one. Odds are though when you play around with Rites and Fetishes you're digging into the Shadow and spirits again, but if you're not? Meh. Game wise it's a resource, just not one hard-wired into every damn thing a werewolf does like it was before. That's kind of the point in part; keep it available to use as much as the player/ST want to, but not smothering everything as a default assumption. <br /> <br /> That's partially why these Instincts are beefed up some and set to be the &quot;bread and butter&quot; foundation; I want folks who focus on these entirely and don't bother with Rites, Fetishes or Numina (I'm leery of calling them Gifts compared to Totem blessings given the common means of gaining them in this) to be good to go without needing to rely on the rest, or spirits and the shadow. Inbuilt allowances to let folks more readily play the game with or without a focus on the Shadow and Spirits to me is a big benefit, not a drawback.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T13:55:12-08:00","id":15605,"title":"","content":"Hmm, on Instincts themselves and the folks that have been looking them over; b are there any stones that have been left unturned for the &quot;bread and butter&quot; powers?<br /> <br /> Keep in mind, there will still be Rites, Fetishes, Totem Blessings, Talens (we're going to tinker with what those are slightly) and spirit Numina (converted when used by the Half-fleshed werewolves) to expand them further, alternate levels (think single Discipline Devotions). With that in mind though, do you folks have any ideas for individual Instincts? Right now the base power set beyond the more spirit-orientated goodies is 7 branches. 10-ish once The Pure get theirs potentially. They don't exactly suffer from lack of diversity, but I'm wondering if a third affinity-for-all Instinct may be worth the while.<br /> <br /> We considered a &quot;Hunting Instincts&quot; but so many of the Instincts in general all cover that in various ways that it seemed redundant and too generalized. Pack Instincts were in a similar boat; still room for it mind you, but we've found it was better off kept as a Merit than an Instinct. <br /> <br /> That said, what about Pure Instincts? Myself and my co-ST have some ideas there, but I want to get something less brain-stormed before posting them up. I want them to diverge more, perhaps one could say seem less 'natural progressions' rather than refinements from existing Instincts.<br /> <br /> Think of it in this manner; we're allowing individual alternate powers much like Promethean Refinements and Single Level Devotions for Instincts. My assumption is that the Pure have either a few alternate levels they hone (or perhaps are taught to focus upon more) that supplant the usual ones. They may even supplant every level 1-5 (in which case, it's effectively a new Instinct) and alter the passive benefit. The prior Gifts they had were one inconsistent mish-mash to say the least, but there were definitely some in there with potential. Without pushing into the line of &quot;Wtf, why isn't that a Numina?&quot; Land and keeping the theme that an Instinct expands upon some core facet of being a werewolf, what ideas do you folks have?<br /> <br /> Infectious Rage from the Rage instinct would make some sense among the Fire-Touched; they may have a different angle with much of Rage Instincts that's more about infecting others in other rabid illness ways and thought patterns. A dominance power that makes individuals more pliant via a &quot;fever&quot; is possible; given they're big on conversion I could see &quot;temporary&quot; converts via Dominance and others, and some frightening potential with Shapeshifting 5 ideas &quot;spreading the holy mark of the chosen among the flock&quot;. I want to play up for these guys a new-ish angle that they're possible more responsible for the notion of &quot;infectious lycanthropy&quot; than the other tribes as a bit more of a spin.<br /> <br /> Purging impurities via an alternate take of Feral Instinct's Predator's endurance would make some for the Ivory Claws, and I could see them having a higher level Dominance effect that's all about purging the influences/control of outside entities on others in there. The empowerment through suffering angle works well within Rage Instincts at well to give them some bite (no pun intended) that Silver Wolf's agony drives them on, and I could see a more reward/painful punishment angle pushed via Dominance Instincts to shift the flavour more.<br /> <br /> Predator Kings are a bit tougher; a lot of there things already are covered between the existing Instincts; given their distaste for humankind they might have some higher level Instinct that cuts out the use of technology, devolving others into feral minds more readily via Rage, Feral or Dominance at lower levels? perhaps some funkiness that exploits Hishu form in some way (reducing time one can stay in it, to boost the duration of Gauru or another in some odd way? A power that empowers the werewolf the more they exist in a more predatory/feral mindset vs thinking like a human?).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T18:13:25-08:00","id":15761,"title":"","content":"I\u2019d be inclined to give each of the Pure Tribes a dedicated Instinct of their own. To the extent that you\u2019re keeping the original mythology in place, there were nine members of the First Pack: five of them conspired to slay Father Wolf (giving rise to the Forsaken Tribes), three retaliated against those five (giving rise to the Pure Tribes), and one is a mystery. If there are separate Instincts favored by each of the Forsaken Tribes, this strongly implies that there ought to be separate Instincts favored by the Pure Tribes: giving them \u201cparallel development paths\u201d for existing Tribes carries the implication that the Pure Tribes are in fact variations of the Forsaken Tribes. That said, I\u2019m perfectly fine with the Pure Instincts being darker aspects of the werewolf condition that self-respecting Forsaken are uncomfortable with: something a bit like Pandoran Transmutations, in that they carry the promise of bringing out the werewolf\u2019s potential in ways that make them monstrously dangerous. As I see the Pure Tribes, each one embodies a different kind of violation of Harmony; and their Instincts ought to be things that likewise violate Harmony, at least when used to their fullest potential. If the Pure manage to maintain high Harmony, it should only be through something like <b>Strix Chronicle</b>\u2019s Banes: without some sort of desensitation against their preferred violations of Harmony, a slide into low Harmony should be all but guaranteed by their chosen lifestyles.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-21T19:16:45-08:00","id":15796,"title":"","content":"Even outside of the mythology/legends (then again, they cease to be that if they're factual, hard-wired facets of the game) most embody some archetype of being a werewolf with a bit of thought. The 3 Pure Tribes even at their core, outside of Harmony violations (and honestly, the current Harmony listing is -not- going to be kept as is on our end) do represent extremism of these archetypes pretty easily as well, with or without a supporting monomyth. On the one end fully divergent Instincts works well, but -reinforcing- the myths via the mechanics isn't really something I see as a motivating factor to do so. I want myths and legends to be just that; not a misuse of the term where it's really &quot;And it's true; the Father Wolf story, the betrayal, the 9 Tribes, all of it, and the mechanics reinforce this&quot;. I see that as boxing options in, rather than opening up the setting for questions, but on the flipside of that, it's nice to bring to the table a set of powers that the assumed PCs aren't going to be familiar with at all to keep them on their toes. I want the myths to still be there including the original presented; I just don't want one given more validity than another via mechanical emphasis if that makes sense.<br /> <br /> I want there to be questions on how accurate they are and their validity; if say, for instance you get a modified Rage-Instinct for the Fire Touched or Predatory Kings; which chain of Honings is the original? Theirs, or the one commonly taught/understood by Forsaken? How can you tell? Some of that is mechanical baggage due to one being presented first rather than an actual setting element; I'm not going by the notion that the default Instincts are the original or 'natural' progressions, though the Forsaken may certainly see it that way and teach their way is somehow more 'right' from a cultural perspective. Even if they're mechanically the default used, it may well be that it's vice-versa. If it makes sense, I don't want to hamstring something into entirely new Instinct sets if they're not actually -needed- for some sort of nebulous in-game symmetry.<br /> <br /> That said.. the issue right now is there hasn't been enough time to give multiple honings for each Instinct level; it's assumed there are. It may well be that the current 1-5s -aren't- the default progression rather than just an example. If they're opened up more it may become less of a problem where one needs to separate what the Pure go after as distinctly, rather than have an example for each Tribe that really encompasses something central via a honing or three. Right now you get some of that clumsiness because each Tribe only has one distinct affinity Instinct; expanding this to include another Affinity Instinct may help but then it comes down to which second Instinct for which Tribe?<br /> <br /> Perhaps just giving them an entirely separate Instinct is the best bet after all; less fuss and muss; symmetry (even if I personally don't see it necessary, it doesn't hurt if it's there) left intact, reinforcing the idea that the Pure have some stark differences. I think you may be right there, Dataweaver; besides, even if it's a separate list there's still ways to play up that say, a Fire Touched Instinct may well have been derived from Rage or vice versa and so on. Thinking on single-Discipline Devotions and how some may be learnable in two different Disciplines, it may well be the same in this instance; some honings may develop from more than once root, which may work best in the end.<br /> <br /> When you have some that have commonalities here and there, it becomes more muddled on who came first, why, and where hidden truths may actually lie. Given Cahalith and the like, I'd honestly like to see more emphasis on digging into history regarding the Forsaken and Pure alike, and less reliance on the validity of their legends, so as long as there are some 'bridges' between the various Instincts, I think it'll still work to suit my chronicle's needs too. In particular, I want the Pure legends and myths to have less in common with the Forsaken's; perhaps some or a lot of overlap, but I actually want to present them as more culturally alien, including in some instances their origin stories to reinforce the divide and to give both sides a finger to point to say &quot;They're not our people even if they once may have been&quot; than they even do now. Whether they're true or not, I do want easy room for tales to exist painting one Tribe as an offshoot of another and something that could be used as fuel for this should it come up.<br /> <br /> The question comes down to; are full, separate sets actually necessary for the Pure, or do they just favour alternate levels? Does which Tribes have what affinities regarding Instincts need to be expanded to encompass 4 rather than 3 given Feral and Shapeshifting are assumed affinity for everyone? Should the Auspice merit (we're using it as such and integrating Aspects into it) give an affinity to an Instinct (I'm a bit unconvinced with this; Forsaken get a free dot of the Auspice merit at creation anyhow)? Or should we just develop 3 more Instincts, perhaps sprinkle some Honings that can be learned via more than one Instinct and go from there? I'm thinking this last one may well be the best bet along with Dataweaver after some thinking, but other perspectives would be appreciated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1LPTOgwgXBVVXxeyQKJOebzMgsN5vUl09k9fwLQVfNaw/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf: the Forsaken Overhaul</a>: A W:tF Shard and House Rules, Pre-Idigam Chronicles and taking different route. Constantly being Updated.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1CSomGcKor9qHrEb7nH15g29587CSzWQY5IgjCRRhdSI/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">New Bloodlines and Blood and Smoke Updates</a>: Homebrew Bloodlines and updates to prior ones.<br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1nHsr9MBiPUrvZLsGDgwnEeEVsxxHFgBqJMUxcCw3BYk/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Belial's Brood Blood and Smoke</a>: An updated take on the Forsworn.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/114-tatterdemalion-king","name":"Tatterdemalion King","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar114_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"241"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}